WEBVTT

NOTE
Fictional reference data for the eval set; all names are placeholders.

1
00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:09.500
<v [PERSON_1]>Thanks for joining. We'd like to understand the [SITE] warehouse before we propose anything.

2
00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:24.000
<v [PERSON_2]>I'm head of logistics at [CUSTOMER]. We are a pharmaceutical wholesaler. [SITE] supplies about nine hundred pharmacies and forty hospitals, twice a day.

3
00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:38.000
<v [PERSON_2]>We need a miniload for the fast-moving totes and a pick-to-light area for about six thousand SKUs. Each tote must be weighed at the end of the line to check the pick.

4
00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:52.000
<v [PERSON_2]>About fifteen percent of our range is cold chain, two to eight degrees. Those orders are picked in a separate cold room and must be packed in validated insulated boxes within twenty minutes of leaving the cold room.

5
00:00:52.500 --> 00:01:05.000
<v [PERSON_3]>Quality assurance here. Everything has to comply with Good Distribution Practice. The system needs computer system validation, and we will expect IQ, OQ and PQ documentation from you.

6
00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:16.000
<v [PERSON_3]>Every pack must have its serial number verified against the national verification system before it leaves the building. We haven't decided whether that check sits in your system or stays in our ERP.

7
00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:27.000
<v [PERSON_4]>IT here. Our ERP is SAP S/4HANA. Orders arrive as IDocs today. The current pharmacy ordering portal sends orders in the evening, so the cut-off at nine p.m. is fixed.

8
00:01:27.500 --> 00:01:38.000
<v [PERSON_4]>We don't know yet how many order lines the new hospital contract will add. Tender results come in February.

9
00:01:38.500 --> 00:01:46.000
<v [PERSON_2]>And batch and expiry dates must be respected: always first-expiry-first-out, and recalled batches must be blocked within minutes.
